we'll take questions for Coach mark  first question here in the front area  newsroom on to see if there's any new  information on clay and Kevon with their  injuries  not really clay said he'll be fine but  you know clay could be half dead and  he'd say he's will see you know he  pulled his hamstring  he thinks it's minor so I don't know  what that means going forward and wound  something with his shoulder and so we'll  see sorry  so I got given all those things apply  what were the keys he thought of the  team ultimately prevailing over those  well you know we I said yesterday and  today that 109 points is plenty to win  the game which is what we had in Game  one but we gave up 118 so is all about  our defense and we held him to 37% and  you know force 15 turnovers and guarded  the 3-point line well so it was  championship defense and that's what  it's gonna take  Nick back left standing Steve Nick free  del ESPN back how would you put into  context the performance DeMarcus gave  you given the fact that he's missed six  weeks and he tore his quad he was great  I mean you know we came in thinking all  right he can you know maybe play 20  minutes and he gave us almost 28 there  was only one time in the game when he  needed a rest which was mid fourth we  gave him a couple minutes and then got  him back in the game but he was  fantastic and you know we needed  everything he gave out there his  rebounding his his toughness his  physical presence you know getting the  ball in the paint and just playing  playing big like he does we needed all  of that so I thought he was fantastic  hey Steve Phil barber Santa Rosa Press  Democrat that 14o run to start the third  quarter we've seen some big third  quarter runs from you guys but how do  you put that one in in context among  the most important you've seen and how  much of that do you think was keyed by  the defensive intensity yeah I mean it  was it was the big point in the game I  thought just staying in the game at at  the end of the second quarter was also  very important I think we were down 12  and a place was going nuts we couldn't  score and Steph and klay both got got  loose and and the game loosened up a  little bit we scored we weren't exactly  making stops but you know we cut the  lead to five and could kind of breathe  at halftime and I think our guys felt  renewed life at that point and came out  and just had a great run to take control  of the game and were able to finish it  out from there it's him in the back  right Steve Tim Reynolds with the AP two  things one you said Steph and klay but  Steph got got loose what was it that was  bothering him early did you ever get any  clarity on that and secondly did you get  did you have a feel at halftime that you  guys were gonna put together one of  those spurts to open a quarter with the  times I mean I couldn't have envisioned  you know forty no but I liked I liked  our position it felt like we should have  been down by a lot more than five and  you know for the first quarter and a  half we had really had a tough time  scoring and so the the last whatever was  four or five six minutes the game  loosened up and and we finally broke  free and started getting some some  buckets we started to look like  ourselves and and so at that point it  just felt better and then you know the  second half we we got it rolling and you  know we ended up with 34 assists which  is you know more like our team and so it  was it was a great win now we got to go  home and and protect our home floor and  we'll see about all the injuries but or  I'm very proud of our team and in  particular all the guys off the bench  Quinn cook hit some huge shots and you  know Bogut came in gave us big  Jerebko as well so it's a hell of an  effort from the bench mark here on the  front left Steve mark Schwartz ESPN  would love to get your impressions of  the final possession where Iguodala hits  the open three first of all the scramble  on Steph the nearly intercepted pass and  the fact that the Raptors allowed a guy  like that to take an open shot and the  fact that he took it with time remaining  on the clock  well I mean you're not gonna let Steph  Curry take the shot  so they double-team Steph and that that  left Andre open and you know he had he  hit another big one earlier in the game  any time Andre can can make a couple  threes it's it's huge for us it loosens  up the game and I thought his play in  the second half was really inspiring at  both ends he did a fantastic job and  he's had a lot of big shots in the  finals before so he was unfazed Tim Jim  Comey athletic Steve you moved clay onto  the Kauai defensive assignment for kind  of freeing up Andre maybe off the ball  do you think that had a difference and  what was the thinking behind that she  just wanted to change the look you know  both teams have a lot of versatility  defensively and both teams have been  kind of switching matchups and changing  the look and we felt that halftime like  it made some sense so we we went with it  and whether that was it or or not I mean  we just got into a good groove  defensively to start that third quarter  and you know so we'll take a look at the  at the tape and assess you know what we  what we see but I was a you know a great  third quarter effort held him to 21  points in that quarter that great to  coach Dan Devine from the ringer  you mentioned needing everything that  DeMarcus was able to give you tonight if  you come out of this game with some  questions about clay and with about  Kevon are you going to need more from  him moving forward do you feel  comfortable with his you know sort of  his health physicality to be able to get  more from him moving forward in the  series from from DeMarcus from DeMarcus  yeah he feels good  in there right now and you know we have  a couple couple days before game 3 so we  do feel confident that we can continue  to get good minutes from him and we're  gonna need them obviously with with all  these injuries in the back Stevie and  Killian with the San Francisco Chronicle  just to go back to Steph for a second  there were reports that he left the game  in the first quarter and that he was  battling some kind of an illness he'd  fill us in on that I think he may have  been a little dehydrated  and that was the word I got he just was  feeling a little bit lightheaded and  went back into the training room and  came back and and was doing much better  so I'm not exactly sure beyond that so  that's all I've got for you last two  quick ones on this side right here Steve  Dan lucky with the Los Angeles Times  can you just kind of expound on sort of  the totality of the team during that run  you mentioned Bogut but like Cooke and  Livingston it seemed like you got  something McKinney from every one of  those guys in the third quarter and how  important is that going to be moving  forwards if you guys are as depleted as  you leave the game well that's what it  takes you know you need your bench no  matter what but in particular when  you've got a lot of injuries so we'll  just continue to go to those guys and  trust them and and they've proven that  they can they can really help us you  know Bogut hadn't played in first game  and three quarters so what he did was  was fantastic out there gave us a little  different look with that lob threat so  we'll just we'll see what we've gotten  and tee it up for game 3 last question  next behind Steve Arash Medina from  Sports Net you mentioned that Andres  unfazed a few years ago so big for you  in the finals what is it about him on  this stage in these big games and the  big moments where he delivers he's just  got a lot of experience he's done  everything in his career he's been in  the Olympics he's won three rings he's  been an all-star  he knows how to play one of the smartest  players I've ever been around  and I think he sensed that that we  needed his production in that second  half and and he came alive thanks Thank  You coach

